# Loaded only by the local Next.js cockpit (`apps/cockpit/.env.local` during
# `next dev`). Copy this file to `.env.local` in this directory, or export the
# same names in the WSL shell. Do not add credentials or secrets.
TRADING_MODE=PAPER

# COURSE-1 PAPER JSON (optional). Default: tests/fixtures/course1_cockpit/live-public-soak
# COCKPIT_ARTIFACT_ROOT=/var/lib/hyperliquid-bot/reconstructable
# COCKPIT_RUN_ID=20260904t001800z-live-paper

# DATA-1A reconstructable capture (read-only). Do not stop a running collector.
# Health JSON is written at stop; growing raw/part-*.parquet files and mtime are
# the live signal until then. DESK/MARKETS/RISK and the first PAPER screen poll
# /api/data1a-capture and /api/venue-capture-health every 5 seconds
# (Cache-Control: no-store). Do not stop the collector to refresh.
#
# TerraPC WSL2 (current 72h retain; Linux filesystem, not /mnt/c).
# Multiple run directories may coexist. Leave venue run_ids unset to auto-detect
# the freshest live retain (claim + fresh raw/part-*.parquet, no health JSON).
# Current operator defaults: HL / Bitvavo / Kraken share
# 20260905t232635z-live-retained. Binance is the post-#58 retain
# 20260906t101559z-live-retained. Do not prefer the stopped earlier BN
# 20260905t235830z-live-retained.
# ARTIFACT_ROOT=$HOME/hyperliquid-artifacts/reconstructable
# DATA1A_RUN_ID=20260905t232635z-live-retained
# DATA1E_RUN_ID=20260905t232635z-live-retained
# DATA1B_RUN_ID=20260905t232635z-live-retained
# DATA1F_RUN_ID=20260906t101559z-live-retained
#
# Equivalent run-id aliases: COCKPIT_DATA1A_RUN_ID, or
# http://127.0.0.1:3000/?data1a_run_id=20260905t232635z-live-retained
#
# Later VPS path-contract root (same file names):
# ARTIFACT_ROOT=/var/lib/hyperliquid-bot/reconstructable
# DATA1A_RUN_ID=20260904t134940z-live-retained
#
# Optional sibling venues on the same ARTIFACT_ROOT (read-only; no secrets).
# Unset run ids auto-detect the freshest live retain, else MISSING. Do not invent zeros.
# The strip polls /api/venue-capture-health every 5 seconds.
# RUNNING requires last raw/part-*.parquet mtime within this window (seconds).
# Host clock must be sane. Soft WARN band is not in v1.
# COCKPIT_CAPTURE_FRESH_MAX_S=180
# Query aliases: ?data1f_run_id= ?data1e_run_id= ?data1b_run_id=
# Picker / query override env. Auto-detect only runs when that venue run_id is unset.
#
# LAN phone (same Wi-Fi, not cellular). Next.js --hostname 0.0.0.0:
#   PORT=3001 pnpm --filter @hyperliquid-bot/cockpit dev:lan
# Then open http://<LAN-IP>:3001 from the phone (the PC's LAN IP on the
# same Wi-Fi, not cellular). Allow the port on the
# Windows/WSL firewall. PORT cannot be set in .env (Next.js boots the HTTP
# server before loading env files).
